```text
PUDC-23-106

October 2, 2023
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to approve the Alliance Addition, 6th Filing Expedited Preliminary Plat, advancing the Final Plat to
the Governing Body.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

•
UDC 2.1.2 Preliminary Plat Approval
•
UDC 2.1.3 Final Plat Approval
•
UDC Article 4 Subdivisions
•
UDC Article 5 Zoning Regulations
•
PlanCheyenne

BACKGROUND:

The applicant is requesting approval of a plat to combine parcels into one large lot for a charter school
development. The resulting lot would be approximately 6.9 acres.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

ANALYSIS OF APPLICATION CONFORMANCE WITH REVIEW CRITERIA:

Should the Planning Commission wish to recommend approval of the Preliminary Plat, the Commission
must make the following findings required in UDC 2.1.2.d – a detailed analysis is below:

1) The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan. (UDC 2.1.2.d.1)

The future land use map within PlanCheyenne identifies this area as Urban Residential.  A
Secondary Use within the Urban Residential category is schools.  The proposed plat would be
compatible with this objective. PlanCheyenne supports the use of existing infrastructure and
timely provision of services (including emergency and education services). This development is
proposed in an area which has largely existing infrastructure and no expansion of infrastructure
is necessary. The property is within the Urban Service Boundary and has access to all utilities.

The application complies with this review criterion.
